     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This issue has been resolved by;",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "Adding the server.properties file to fedora-client.jar and fedora-messaging.jar so that property values can be resolved correctly",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "Adding an option in the messaging client to start the connection to the messaging provider asynchronously, and updating GSearch to use this option. When starting the UpdateListener in GSearch, if a connection cannot be made a wait and retry will occur in a separate thread. This will allow Fedora to start up and make the messaging provider available.",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         }
        ],
        "type": "bulletList"
       }
      ],
